From: Yanghan Ye <yyh94306@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: mt7996: release HIF2 on all probe errors

Release the acquired HIF2 device reference from the common free-device
exit. Early primary WED and IRQ errors bypass the old free-hif2 label,
so releasing there leaked the reference on those failures. Preserve the
existing IRQ, WED and device cleanup ordering and do not run hardware
cleanup before its work items have been initialized.

Signed-off-by: Yanghan Ye <yyh94306@gmail.com>
Assisted-by: Codex:GPT-5.6-sol
Index: mt76/mt7996/pci.c
===================================================================
--- mt76.orig/mt7996/pci.c	2026-10-09 19:18:01.999531796 -0700
+++ mt76/mt7996/pci.c	2026-10-09 19:44:33.430386778 -0700
@@ -220,8 +220,6 @@
 			pci_free_irq_vectors(hif2_dev);
 	}
 free_hif2:
-	if (dev->hif2)
-		put_device(dev->hif2->dev);
 	devm_free_irq(mdev->dev, irq, dev);
 free_wed_or_irq_vector:
 	if (mtk_wed_device_active(&dev->mt76.mmio.wed))
@@ -229,6 +227,7 @@
 	else
 		pci_free_irq_vectors(pdev);
 free_device:
+	mt7996_put_hif2(dev->hif2);
 	mt76_free_device(&dev->mt76);
 
 	return ret;
